<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ Refining lifts 1996 operating earnings.</title>
<headline>NZ Refining lifts 1996 operating earnings.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31.</p>
<p>			(million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   46.54 vs 51.26</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			 194    vs 214</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			  85    vs 100</p>
<p>    Total div for yr (cents)	160    vs 150</p>
<p>    Turnover			    279.8  vs 278.6</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			70.5  vs  72.5</p>
<p>    Tax				    23.98 vs  21.24</p>
<p>    Abnormals			     nil  vs  12.13 credit</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)   24.00 vs  same</p>
<p>    Dividend carried 41.0 cps imputation credit.</p>
<p>    Pay date April 24</p>
<p>    Reg date April 11</p>
<p>    Ex div   April 14</p>
<p>    Note - The New Zealand Refining Co Ltd, an oil refiner, is owned by local units of Mobil Corp (19.2 percent), The British Petroleum Co Plc (23.66 percent), Royal Dutch Petroleum Co (17.14 percent) and 10.0 percent by Caltex Petroleum Corp. Petrocorp, a unit of Fletcher Challenge Ltd, owns 14.11 percent.</p>
<p>--Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
